 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n1. You define a time-of-use interface and select it for execution in EDM.\n\nYou use time-of-use formulas with a formula class. SAP provides formula classes for aggregation and determination of peak\ndemand values. You can also define your own formula classes.\n\n2. You import the profile values in the SAP system - for example, using BAP! BAPI_ISUPROFILE IMPORT.\n\n3. You execute billing as normal.\n\nConstraints\n\nBilling in combination with period-end billing, backbilling, or billing in advance is only possible with restrictions. Operands that\nreceive values from the time-of-use interface can only be used in rate steps that belong to the periodic billing period.\n\nTime-of-Use Interface\n\nUse\n\nYou can use the time-of-use interface to aggregate the profiles for billing. The interface contains the periods (for example, a\nweekday in summer 08:00 17:59) and time-of-use formulas (for example, consumption above limit value), which are used to\nprocess the profile values transfer them to the rate for billing. The following figure uses an example to illustrate this:\n\nRate\n\nTime-of-Use Interfaces                   Intervall Length: 10 mins\n\nSeason Day Group       From\u2014To Formula           Output Parameters       Result Param.             Operand\n\nSummer |\\Weekday (Mo\u2014 }00:00-07\u00b059|5678 Cons.      Consumption           OFF_PEAKses4eeeerdeem CONS OFFPEAK\n08:00-17:\u00b059|5679 Demand = |Maximum            DEM_MAX\n\n5680 Cons. over/|Consumption on-peak     ON_PEAK\nunder limit        and peak load            CRIT_PEAK :\n\n.\n.\n\n18:00\u201423:59 |5678 Cons.       Consumption              OFF_PEAK=:\n\nWeekend _[00.00-23.58 [5678 Cons [Consumption ___OFF_PEAK-*\n\n>\u00bb CONS_ONPEAK\n\nseksedes\n\nPublicHoliday [0\n\nEe a a es\nWinter [Weekdays ff\n\nExample of a Time-of-Use Interface\n\nInterval Length\n\nThe interval length for the time-of-use interface must be the same as the interval length for the profile.\n\nPeriods and Formulas\n\nIn the example above the year is divided into summer and winter. In summer you can choose from weekdays, weekends, public\nholidays, and exception days (such as the football world cup final day). Whilst for weekdays, consumption and demand are\ncalculated using other formulas based on the time of day, only consumption is calculated for weekends.\n\nYou can define how the year can be divided into sections in Customizing. You can also map the year as a season group, or as a\ngroup with the season types summer, winter, and transition. For each season, you determine in the time-of-use interface, the type\n\nof day (Monday-Sunday, public holiday, exception day) on which you expect consumption behaviour to be different. These are the\n",
